  "definition": "Data Protection Regulation refers to the legal and policy frameworks\u2014such as the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and the UK Data Protection Act 2018\u2014that govern how personal data may be collected, processed, stored, and shared by organisations. These regulations impose obligations around lawful basis for processing, data subject rights, cross-border transfer restrictions, and mandatory breach notification, creating compliance requirements for AI systems that handle personal data.",
